{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2815334","formula":"C₂₀H₃₇NaO₇S","hill":"C20H37NaO7S","elements":["H","C","O","Na","S"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":37.0,"O":7.0,"S":1.0,"Na":1.0},"names":{"en":"Docusate sodium","ru":"Докузат"},"descriptions":{"en":"Docusate is the common chemical and pharmaceutical name of the anion bis(2-ethylhexyl) sulfosuccinate, also commonly called dioctyl sulfosuccinate (DOSS). Salts of this anion, especially docusate sodium, are widely used in medicine as an emollient laxative and as stool softeners, by mouth or rectally. Some studies state that docusate is not more effective than a placebo for improving constipation.","ru":"Докузат, также известный как докузатные соли или диоктилсульфосукцинат, является слабительным средством для размягчения стула и используется для лечения запоров. Считается, что это хороший выбор для детей с твердым стулом. Однако, применение при запорах плохо подкреплено доказательствами."},"fame":26,"pubchemCid":23673837,"mass":444.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCC(CC)COC(=O)CC(C(=O)OCC(CC)CCCC)S(=O)(=O)[O-].[Na+]","inchikey":"APSBXTVYXVQYAB-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"sodium 1,4-bis(2-ethylhexoxy)-1,4-dioxobutane-2-sulfonate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"23673837","atoms":66,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.491,"y":3.264,"z":1.323,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.807,"y":1.809,"z":1.009,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.678,"y":1.157,"z":0.209,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.963,"y":-0.302,"z":-0.173,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.27,"y":-1.347,"z":0.733,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.742,"y":-1.334,"z":2.199,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.206,"y":-1.693,"z":2.413,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.4,"y":-2.76,"z":0.126,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.732,"y":-2.847,"z":-1.143,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.383,"y":-3.023,"z":-1.09,"el":"C"},{"x":0.26,"y":-3.169,"z":-0.058,"el":"O"},{"x":0.216,"y":-2.999,"z":-2.4